IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc3-freezing.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART II.1 Terrorism, "Freezing of Property": sections 83.08 to 83.12 (the prohibition on dealing,
-- exemptions, the duty to disclose, the duty to audit and report, and the offence of contravening them).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), written by part agent ccc3 from the text alone. The text is a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
--
-- READING A RESULT (rule of 2026-10-29): as in `ccc3-interpretation.l4`. A prohibition or a duty limited by its own wording ("knowingly", "No person in Canada and no
-- Canadian outside Canada", "that they know") answers NOTHING outside the limit; JUST FALSE is kept for a closed list, a flat negative and an offence whose element is unmet
-- (fork F-ccc3-1). The prohibitions and duties are also regulative rules (PARTY ... SHANT / MUST), run with #TRACE and checked by `work/trace_check.py`;
-- the same duty is also a decision function, because an #ASSERT cannot compare a DEONTIC value on the stable binary. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- The regulative rules are written over the core's `Party` (`the accused`, `an organization`), as the core intends.

§ `Section 83.08 -- Freezing of property`

-- (1) "No person in Canada and no Canadian outside Canada shall knowingly (a) deal ...; (b) enter into or facilitate ...; or (c) provide any financial or other related services ...".
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-19 | s 83.08(1) the person is barred from the act | s 83.08(1)*
-- src:1504 | Freezing of Property
-- src:1505 | Freezing of property
-- src:1506 | 83.08 (1) No person in Canada and no Canadian outside Canada shall knowingly
-- src:1507 | (a) deal directly or indirectly in any property that is owned or controlled by or on behalf of a terrorist group;
-- src:1508 | (b) enter into or facilitate, directly or indirectly, any transaction in respect of property referred to in paragraph (a); or
-- src:1509 | (c) provide any financial or other related services in respect of property referred to in paragraph (a) to, for the benefit of or at the direction of a terrorist group.
@ref s 83.08(1) (src:1504-1509)
DECLARE `s 83.08(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.08(1)(a) deals, directly or indirectly, in property that is owned or controlled by or on behalf of a terrorist group`
    `s 83.08(1)(b) enters into or facilitates, directly or indirectly, a transaction in respect of that property`
    `s 83.08(1)(c) provides financial or other related services in respect of that property to, for the benefit of or at the direction of a terrorist group`
    `s 83.08(1) does none of those things`

@ref s 83.08(1) (src:1504-1509)
GIVEN `the person is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a Canadian, by s 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      act IS A `s 83.08(1) act`
      `the person does it knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is owned or controlled by or on behalf of the group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group is a terrorist group, by s 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.08(1) the person is barred from the act` MEANS
    IF     act EQUALS `s 83.08(1) does none of those things`
        OR NOT `the person does it knowingly`
        OR NOT `the property is owned or controlled by or on behalf of the group`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall knowingly"
    ELSE IF `the person is in Canada`
         THEN `the answer on the group`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the person is a Canadian, by s 83.01(1)`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `the answer on the group`
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person in Canada and no Canadian outside Canada"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a Canadian is for s 83.01(1)
    WHERE
        `the answer on the group` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the group is a terrorist group, by s 83.01(1)`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "property that is owned or controlled by or on behalf of a terrorist group"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the group is a terrorist group is for s 83.01(1)

-- The same prohibition as a regulative rule: the person SHANT do any of the three things. The text gives no time limit and no consequence, so there is none here.
@ref s 83.08(1) (src:1504-1509)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 83.08(1) act`
`s 83.08(1) the prohibition` MEANS
        (PARTY `the accused` SHANT `s 83.08(1)(a) deals, directly or indirectly, in property that is owned or controlled by or on behalf of a terrorist group`)
    RAND (PARTY `the accused` SHANT `s 83.08(1)(b) enters into or facilitates, directly or indirectly, a transaction in respect of that property`)
    RAND (PARTY `the accused` SHANT `s 83.08(1)(c) provides financial or other related services in respect of that property to, for the benefit of or at the direction of a terrorist group`)

-- (2) an immunity from civil liability.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.08(2) the person is not liable in the civil action | s 83.08(2)
-- src:1510 | No civil liability
-- src:1511 | (2) A person who acts reasonably in taking, or omitting to take, measures to comply with subsection (1) shall not be liable in any civil action arising from having taken or omitted to take the measures, if they took all reasonable steps to satisfy themselves that the relevant property was owned or controlled by or on behalf of a terrorist group.
@ref s 83.08(2) (src:1510-1511)
GIVEN `the person acts reasonably in taking, or omitting to take, measures to comply with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person took all reasonable steps to satisfy themselves that the relevant property was owned or controlled by or on behalf of a terrorist group` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.08(2) the person is not liable in the civil action` MEANS
    IF `the person acts reasonably in taking, or omitting to take, measures to comply with subsection (1)` AND `the person took all reasonable steps to satisfy themselves that the relevant property was owned or controlled by or on behalf of a terrorist group`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not be liable in any civil action arising from having taken or omitted to take the measures, if they took all reasonable steps"

§ `Section 83.09 -- Exemptions`

-- (1) A power of the Minister, or a person designated by the Minister, limited by its own wording to a person in Canada or a Canadian outside Canada, a specified activity or transaction (or a class of them) that section 83.08 prohibits.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.09(1) the Minister or a designated person may authorize the activity or transaction | s 83.09(1)
-- src:1512 | Exemptions
-- src:1513 | 83.09 (1) The Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness, or a person designated by him or her, may authorize any person in Canada or any Canadian outside Canada to carry out a specified activity or transaction that is prohibited by section 83.08, or a class of such activities or transactions.
@ref s 83.09(1) (src:1512-1513)
GIVEN `the person is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a Canadian, by s 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the activity or transaction is specified, or is a class of such activities or transactions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prohibited by section 83.08` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.09(1) the Minister or a designated person may authorize the activity or transaction` MEANS
    IF     `the activity or transaction is specified, or is a class of such activities or transactions`
       AND `it is prohibited by section 83.08`
       AND (`the person is in Canada` OR `the person is a Canadian, by s 83.01(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may authorize any person in Canada or any Canadian outside Canada to carry out a specified activity or transaction that is prohibited by section 83.08"

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.09(2) the Minister or a designated person may make the authorization subject to terms and conditions; s 83.09(2) the Minister or a designated person may amend, suspend, revoke or reinstate the authorization | s 83.09(2)
-- src:1514 | Ministerial authorization
-- src:1515 | (2) The Minister, or a person designated by him or her, may make the authorization subject to any terms and conditions that are required in their opinion and may amend, suspend, revoke or reinstate it.
@ref s 83.09(2) (src:1514-1515)
GIVEN `in their opinion the terms and conditions are required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.09(2) the Minister or a designated person may make the authorization subject to terms and conditions` MEANS
    IF `in their opinion the terms and conditions are required`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any terms and conditions that are required in their opinion"

@ref s 83.09(2) (src:1514-1515)
GIVEN `the authorization was given under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.09(2) the Minister or a designated person may amend, suspend, revoke or reinstate the authorization` MEANS
    IF `the authorization was given under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may amend, suspend, revoke or reinstate it"

-- (3) ENTITLED-group: "are entitled to the same ranking ...", "other than terrorist groups or their agents" (a case-by-case "(other than X)": the excluded holder is the text's no; fork F-ccc3-9).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-9,F-ccc3-14 | s 83.09(3) the rights and interests are entitled to the same ranking | s 83.09(3)
-- src:1516 | Existing equities maintained
-- src:1517 | (3) All secured and unsecured rights and interests in the frozen property that are held by persons, other than terrorist groups or their agents, are entitled to the same ranking that they would have been entitled to had the property not been frozen.
@ref s 83.09(3) (src:1516-1517)
GIVEN `the rights or interests are secured or unsecured rights and interests in the frozen property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder is a terrorist group or the agent of one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.09(3) the rights and interests are entitled to the same ranking` MEANS
    IF NOT `the rights or interests are secured or unsecured rights and interests in the frozen property`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "All secured and unsecured rights and interests in the frozen property"
    ELSE IF `the holder is a terrorist group or the agent of one`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that are held by persons, other than terrorist groups or their agents"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (4) An exception for a person involved in an activity authorized under (1): "is not subject to sections 83.08, 83.1 and 83.11 if the terms or conditions ... are met".
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.09(4) the other person is not subject to sections 83.08, 83.1 and 83.11 | s 83.09(4)
-- src:1518 | Third party involvement
-- src:1519 | (4) If a person has obtained an authorization under subsection (1), any other person involved in carrying out the activity or transaction, or class of activities or transactions, to which the authorization relates is not subject to sections 83.08, 83.1 and 83.11 if the terms or conditions of the authorization that are imposed under subsection (2), if any, are met.
@ref s 83.09(4) (src:1518-1519)
GIVEN `a person has obtained an authorization under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is involved in carrying out the activity or transaction, or class of activities or transactions, to which the authorization relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms or conditions of the authorization that are imposed under subsection (2), if any, are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.09(4) the other person is not subject to sections 83.08, 83.1 and 83.11` MEANS
    IF     `a person has obtained an authorization under subsection (1)`
       AND `the other person is involved in carrying out the activity or transaction, or class of activities or transactions, to which the authorization relates`
       AND `the terms or conditions of the authorization that are imposed under subsection (2), if any, are met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is not subject to sections 83.08, 83.1 and 83.11 if the terms or conditions of the authorization that are imposed under subsection (2), if any, are met"

§ `Section 83.1 -- Disclosure`

-- (1) "Every person in Canada and every Canadian outside Canada shall disclose without delay to the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service
-- (a) the existence of property in their possession or control that they know is owned or controlled by or on behalf of a terrorist group; and (b) information about a transaction or proposed transaction in respect of property referred to in paragraph (a)."
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-19 | s 83.1(1)(a) the person must disclose the existence of the property; s 83.1(1)(b) the person must disclose information about the transaction | s 83.1(1)*
-- src:1520 | Disclosure
-- src:1521 | 83.1 (1) Every person in Canada and every Canadian outside Canada shall disclose without delay to the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service
-- src:1522 | (a) the existence of property in their possession or control that they know is owned or controlled by or on behalf of a terrorist group; and
-- src:1523 | (b) information about a transaction or proposed transaction in respect of property referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref s 83.1(1) (src:1520-1523)
GIVEN `the person is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a Canadian, by s 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the property is in the person’s possession or control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that it is owned or controlled by or on behalf of the group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group is a terrorist group, by s 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.1(1)(a) the person must disclose the existence of the property` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the property is in the person’s possession or control` AND `the person knows that it is owned or controlled by or on behalf of the group`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "property in their possession or control that they know is owned or controlled by or on behalf of a terrorist group"
    ELSE IF `the person is in Canada`
         THEN `the answer on the group`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the person is a Canadian, by s 83.01(1)`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `the answer on the group`
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person in Canada and every Canadian outside Canada"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a Canadian is for s 83.01(1)
    WHERE
        `the answer on the group` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the group is a terrorist group, by s 83.01(1)`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "owned or controlled by or on behalf of a terrorist group"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the group is a terrorist group is for s 83.01(1)

@ref s 83.1(1) (src:1520-1523)
GIVEN `the person must disclose the existence of the property, by s 83.1(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has information about a transaction or proposed transaction in respect of that property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.1(1)(b) the person must disclose information about the transaction` MEANS
    IF `the person has information about a transaction or proposed transaction in respect of that property`
    THEN `the person must disclose the existence of the property, by s 83.1(1)(a)`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "information about a transaction or proposed transaction in respect of property referred to in paragraph (a)"

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the person MUST make each disclosure "without delay". The text gives no number of days, so there is no WITHIN, and none is invented.
@ref s 83.1(1) (src:1520-1523)
DECLARE `s 83.1(1) disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.1(1)(a) discloses the existence of the property to the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service`
    `s 83.1(1)(b) discloses information about a transaction or proposed transaction to the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service`

@ref s 83.1(1) (src:1520-1523)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 83.1(1) disclosure`
`s 83.1(1) the duty to disclose` MEANS
        (PARTY `the accused` MUST `s 83.1(1)(a) discloses the existence of the property to the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service` HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "the existence of the property was not disclosed without delay")
    RAND (PARTY `the accused` MUST `s 83.1(1)(b) discloses information about a transaction or proposed transaction to the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service` HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "the information about the transaction was not disclosed without delay")

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.1(2) no criminal or civil proceedings lie against the person | s 83.1(2)
-- src:1524 | Immunity
-- src:1525 | (2) No criminal or civil proceedings lie against a person for disclosure made in good faith under subsection (1).
@ref s 83.1(2) (src:1524-1525)
GIVEN `the disclosure was made in good faith under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.1(2) no criminal or civil proceedings lie against the person` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure was made in good faith under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for disclosure made in good faith under subsection (1)"

§ `Section 83.11 -- Audit`

-- (1) The entities that must determine, on a continuing basis, whether they hold property of a listed entity. The text names nine kinds; a tenth is "none of those" (the list is a duty list without "only").
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.11(1) the entity must determine whether it is in possession or control of the property | s 83.11(1)*
-- src:1526 | Audit
-- src:1527 | 83.11 (1) The following entities must determine on a continuing basis whether they are in possession or control of property owned or controlled by or on behalf of a listed entity:
-- src:1528 | (a) authorized foreign banks within the meaning of section 2 of the Bank Act in respect of their business in Canada, or banks to which that Act applies;
-- src:1529 | (b) cooperative credit societies, savings and credit unions and caisses populaires regulated by a provincial Act and associations regulated by the Cooperative Credit Associations Act;
-- src:1530 | (c) foreign companies within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Insurance Companies Act in respect of their insurance business in Canada;
-- src:1531 | (c.1) companies, provincial companies and societies within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Insurance Companies Act;
-- src:1532 | (c.2) fraternal benefit societies regulated by a provincial Act in respect of their insurance activities, and insurance companies and other entities engaged in the business of insuring risks that are regulated by a provincial Act;
-- src:1533 | (d) companies to which the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies;
-- src:1534 | (e) trust companies regulated by a provincial Act;
-- src:1535 | (f) loan companies regulated by a provincial Act; and
-- src:1536 | (g) entities authorized under provincial legislation to engage in the business of dealing in securities, or to provide portfolio management or investment counselling services.
@ref s 83.11(1) (src:1526-1536)
DECLARE `s 83.11(1) entity` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.11(1)(a) an authorized foreign bank within the meaning of section 2 of the Bank Act in respect of its business in Canada, or a bank to which that Act applies`
    `s 83.11(1)(b) a cooperative credit society, savings and credit union or caisse populaire regulated by a provincial Act, or an association regulated by the Cooperative Credit Associations Act`
    `s 83.11(1)(c) a foreign company within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Insurance Companies Act in respect of its insurance business in Canada`
    `s 83.11(1)(c.1) a company, provincial company or society within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Insurance Companies Act`
    `s 83.11(1)(c.2) a fraternal benefit society regulated by a provincial Act in respect of its insurance activities, or an insurance company or other entity engaged in the business of insuring risks that is regulated by a provincial Act`
    `s 83.11(1)(d) a company to which the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies`
    `s 83.11(1)(e) a trust company regulated by a provincial Act`
    `s 83.11(1)(f) a loan company regulated by a provincial Act`
    `s 83.11(1)(g) an entity authorized under provincial legislation to engage in the business of dealing in securities, or to provide portfolio management or investment counselling services`
    `s 83.11(1) an entity of none of those kinds`

@ref s 83.11(1) (src:1526-1536)
GIVEN entity IS A `s 83.11(1) entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.11(1) the entity must determine whether it is in possession or control of the property` MEANS
    CONSIDER entity
    WHEN `s 83.11(1) an entity of none of those kinds` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following entities must determine on a continuing basis"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2) "Subject to the regulations, every entity ... must report, within the period specified by regulation or, if no period is specified, monthly, to the principal agency or body that supervises or regulates it ... either
-- (a) that it is not in possession or control of any property referred to in subsection (1), or (b) that it is in possession or control of such property, in which case it must also report the number of persons, contracts or accounts involved and the total value of the property."
-- The period specified by regulation is not in the text (it is an input); "monthly" is one calendar month (`add months`).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-10 | s 83.11(2) the day by which the next report is due; s 83.11(2) the report is complete; s 83.11(2) the duty to report | s 83.11(2)*
-- src:1537 | Monthly report
-- src:1538 | (2) Subject to the regulations, every entity referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (g) must report, within the period specified by regulation or, if no period is specified, monthly, to the principal agency or body that supervises or regulates it under federal or provincial law either
-- src:1539 | (a) that it is not in possession or control of any property referred to in subsection (1), or
-- src:1540 | (b) that it is in possession or control of such property, in which case it must also report the number of persons, contracts or accounts involved and the total value of the property.
@ref s 83.11(2) (src:1537-1540)
GIVEN `the day of the last report` IS A DATE
      `the period specified by regulation, in days, if one is specified` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 83.11(2) the day by which the next report is due` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period specified by regulation, in days, if one is specified`
    WHEN JUST days THEN `the day of the last report` PLUS days
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `add months` `the day of the last report` 1

@ref s 83.11(2) (src:1537-1540)
GIVEN `the report says that the entity is not in possession or control of any property referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report says that the entity is in possession or control of such property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report gives the number of persons, contracts or accounts involved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report gives the total value of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.11(2) the report is complete` MEANS
    IF `the report says that the entity is not in possession or control of any property referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the report says that the entity is in possession or control of such property` AND `the report gives the number of persons, contracts or accounts involved` AND `the report gives the total value of the property`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in which case it must also report the number of persons, contracts or accounts involved and the total value of the property"

@ref s 83.11(2) (src:1537-1540)
DECLARE `s 83.11(2) report` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.11(2)(a) reports that it is not in possession or control of any property referred to in subsection (1)`
    `s 83.11(2)(b) reports that it is in possession or control of such property, with the number of persons, contracts or accounts involved and the total value of the property`

-- The period (in days on this rule's clock) is an input: a regulation sets it, or, if none, it is monthly, which the caller turns into days with the function above.
@ref s 83.11(2) (src:1537-1540)
GIVEN `the number of days within which the report is due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 83.11(2) report`
`s 83.11(2) the duty to report` MEANS
        (PARTY `an organization` MUST `s 83.11(2)(a) reports that it is not in possession or control of any property referred to in subsection (1)` WITHIN `the number of days within which the report is due` HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY `an organization` BECAUSE "no report was made within the period")
    ROR (PARTY `an organization` MUST `s 83.11(2)(b) reports that it is in possession or control of such property, with the number of persons, contracts or accounts involved and the total value of the property` WITHIN `the number of days within which the report is due` HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY `an organization` BECAUSE "no report was made within the period")

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.11(3) no criminal or civil proceedings lie against the person for the report | s 83.11(3)
-- src:1541 | Immunity
-- src:1542 | (3) No criminal or civil proceedings lie against a person for making a report in good faith under subsection (2).
@ref s 83.11(3) (src:1541-1542)
GIVEN `the report was made in good faith under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.11(3) no criminal or civil proceedings lie against the person for the report` MEANS
    IF `the report was made in good faith under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for making a report in good faith under subsection (2)"

§ `Section 83.12 -- Offences: freezing of property, disclosure or audit`

-- (1) "Every person who contravenes any of sections 83.08, 83.1 and 83.11 is guilty of an offence and liable (a) on conviction on indictment, ... not more than 10 years; or (b) on summary conviction, to a fine of not more than $100,000
-- or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day, or to both."
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-1 | s 83.12(1) the person is guilty of the offence; s 83.12(1) the class of the offence; s 83.12(1) the punishments of the offence | s 83.12(1)*
-- src:1547 | Offences — freezing of property, disclosure or audit
-- src:1548 | 83.12 (1) Every person who contravenes any of sections 83.08, 83.1 and 83.11 is guilty of an offence and liable
-- src:1549 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:1550 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine of not more than $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day, or to both.
@ref s 83.12(1) (src:1547-1550)
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 83.08` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person contravenes section 83.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person contravenes section 83.11` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.12(1) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes section 83.08` OR `the person contravenes section 83.1` OR `the person contravenes section 83.11`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who contravenes any of sections 83.08, 83.1 and 83.11 is guilty of an offence"

@ref s 83.12(1) (src:1548-1550)
`s 83.12(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- Two limbs: (a) on indictment; (b) on summary conviction (a fine of not more than $100,000, or imprisonment of not more than two years less a day, or both).
@ref s 83.12(1) (src:1548-1550)
`s 83.12(1) the punishments of the offence` MEANS
    LIST
        (Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`),
        (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`), `no imprisonment is stated`, (`a fine of` 100000), `no fine is stated`)
